declare n int;
begin
  if exists (select 1 from benchmark_workouts where slug in ('nukes', 'paul', 'pike', 'ralph', 'rich', 'ship', 't', 'the-lyon', 'tk', 'wood', 'zimmerman', 'jacks-triangle')) then raise exception 'slug exists'; end if;
  insert into benchmark_workouts (name, slug, category, subcategory, format, scheme, duration_estimate, difficulty, body_focus, equipment, scoring_type, description, movements, scoring_notes, tips, coaching_tips, scaling_notes, faqs, youtube_url) values
  ('Nukes',
   'nukes',
   'hero',
   null,
   'Other',
   '3 Timed Segments (8/10/12 min)',
   '30 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['running','barbell']::text[],
   'total_reps',
   'Nukes honors U.S. Marine Corps Capt. Matthew "Nukes" Manoukian, 29, of Los Altos Hills, California, of the 1st Marine Special Operations Battalion. He died on Aug. 10, 2012, in Sangin District, Afghanistan, after being shot by an Afghan policeman.

The workout is three timed windows done back to back with no rest. In 8 minutes you run a mile and then deadlift (315 lb / 205 lb) for max reps. In the next 10 minutes you run a mile and then power clean (225 lb / 155 lb). In the last 12 minutes you run a mile and then overhead squat (135 lb / 95 lb). A fast mile buys lifting time, but every lift is heavy and starts on tired legs and lungs.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Segment 1 has an 8-minute window. Every second you save on the run is time for deadlifts."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "Max reps", "tip": "Use the time left in the 8 minutes. Brace hard and reset at the floor when your back starts to round.", "rx_men": "315 lb", "rx_women": "205 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Segment 2 starts right away with a 10-minute window. Your legs will feel the deadlifts, so settle in fast."}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "Max reps", "tip": "Quick singles with a fast elbow turnover are safer than touch-and-go reps at this load.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Segment 3 starts right away with a 12-minute window. Hold enough back to stay steady overhead."}, {"name": "Overhead Squats", "reps": "Max reps", "tip": "Wide grip, active shoulders and a full squat on every rep. Rack the bar before it drifts forward.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total reps of deadlifts, power cleans and overhead squats. Each segment starts with a 1-mile run, and any time left in the window goes to the lift.',
   '["A faster mile means more time to lift", "Singles on the heavy lifts are fine", "The next window starts right away, so move straight to the run"]'::jsonb,
   '["Run the first mile hard but controlled, since the deadlift window is only 8 minutes.", "Set up the three bars before you start so you never lose time changing plates.", "On the deadlifts and power cleans, a steady pace of quick singles usually beats long sets you have to stop in the middle of.", "Keep your eyes forward and your core tight on the overhead squats so the bar stays over your mid-foot.", "If you cannot finish a mile inside a window, that window scores zero reps, so pick a load and pace that leaves you time to lift."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut the runs to 800 m–1,200 m so you have real lifting time in each window. Lower the loads to about 50–60% of your one-rep max for each lift, for example 185 lb / 125 lb deadlifts, 135 lb / 95 lb power cleans and 75 lb / 55 lb overhead squats. Front squats can replace overhead squats if your shoulders do not allow a stable overhead position.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Nukes workout?", "answer": "Three windows with no rest between them: in 8 minutes, a 1-mile run then max deadlifts (315 lb / 205 lb); in 10 minutes, a 1-mile run then max power cleans (225 lb / 155 lb); in 12 minutes, a 1-mile run then max overhead squats (135 lb / 95 lb)."}, {"question": "How is Nukes scored?", "answer": "Your score is the total reps of all three lifts. You only get to lift once you finish the mile in that window."}, {"question": "Who was Nukes?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Corps Capt. Matthew \"Nukes\" Manoukian, 29, of the 1st Marine Special Operations Battalion. He died on Aug. 10, 2012, in Sangin District, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "How long does Nukes take?", "answer": "30 minutes. The three windows of 8, 10 and 12 minutes run back to back."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GNETNCJxLV0'),
  ('Paul',
   'paul',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '5 Rounds For Time',
   '20–30 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['jumpRope','pullUpBar','barbell']::text[],
   'time',
   'Paul honors Pittsburgh Police Officer Paul John Rizzo Domenic Sciullo II, 36. He was shot and killed in the line of duty on April 4, 2009, while responding to a domestic disturbance call.

You complete five rounds of 50 double-unders, 35 knees-to-elbows and a 20-yard overhead walk with a barbell (185 lb / 125 lb). That adds up to 250 double-unders, 175 knees-to-elbows and 100 yards under a heavy bar. The rope and the hanging work both drain your grip and shoulders, and then you have to press a heavy bar overhead and hold it there while you walk. Getting the bar up safely each round is part of the challenge.',
   '[{"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "50", "tip": "Stay tall, keep the jumps small and turn the rope from your wrists."}, {"name": "Knees-to-Elbows", "reps": "35", "tip": "Break into sets of 7 to 12 before your grip forces a long rest."}, {"name": "Overhead Walk", "reps": "20 yd", "tip": "Lock out the bar with your biceps by your ears and take short, steady steps.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Small sets on the knees-to-elbows protect your grip", "Get the bar overhead the same way every round", "Short steps and a hard brace on the walk"]'::jsonb,
   '["Plan your knees-to-elbows sets before you start, such as 12, 12, 11, and stick to them.", "Shake out your grip on the way to the bar so you can hold it overhead without rushing.", "Clean the bar and push jerk or split jerk it overhead, then lock your elbows before the first step.", "Squeeze your glutes and keep your ribs down on the walk so your lower back does not arch.", "If the bar drifts forward, stop, reset and keep walking rather than chasing it."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 95 lb / 65 lb, or carry a dumbbell or kettlebell in each hand overhead. Replace double-unders with 100 single-unders, and use hanging knee raises or V-ups in place of knees-to-elbows. Cut to three rounds if five would take more than about 30 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Paul workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of 50 double-unders, 35 knees-to-elbows and a 20-yard overhead walk with a barbell (185 lb / 125 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Paul?", "answer": "250 double-unders, 175 knees-to-elbows and 100 yards of overhead walking."}, {"question": "Who was Paul?", "answer": "Pittsburgh Police Officer Paul John Rizzo Domenic Sciullo II, 36, who was shot and killed in the line of duty on April 4, 2009."}, {"question": "What do I walk with overhead?", "answer": "A loaded barbell, 185 lb for men and 125 lb for women. Scale with a lighter bar or with dumbbells or kettlebells."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mqHvlMnTKYg'),
  ('Pike',
   'pike',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '5 Rounds For Time',
   '30–45 min',
   'advanced',
   'upper-body',
   array['barbell','rings','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'Pike honors U.S. Navy Chief Petty Officer Christian Michael Pike, 31, of Peoria, Arizona, a Chief Cryptologic Technician with a West Coast-based Naval Special Warfare unit. He died on March 12, 2013, in Landstuhl, Germany, of combat injuries sustained days earlier in the Maiwand District of Kandahar, Afghanistan, and was posthumously awarded the Bronze Star with Valor.

You complete five rounds of 20 thrusters (75 lb / 55 lb), 10 strict ring dips, 20 push-ups, 10 strict handstand push-ups and a 50 m bear crawl. Every movement loads the shoulders and triceps, and the strict dips and handstand push-ups allow no kip. Pressing endurance runs out fast.',
   '[{"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "20", "tip": "The bar is light, so use your legs and keep a steady rhythm. Break before your shoulders give out.", "rx_men": "75 lb", "rx_women": "55 lb"}, {"name": "Strict Ring Dips", "reps": "10", "tip": "No kip. Lower until your shoulders are below your elbows, then press to full lockout."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a straight body line. Small sets from the first round."}, {"name": "Strict Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "No kip. Head to the floor and arms locked at the top. Singles are fine once you slow down."}, {"name": "Bear Crawls", "reps": "50 m", "tip": "Hips low and short steps. Your shoulders will be tired, so keep moving slowly rather than stopping."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the pressing early and often", "Strict means no kip on dips and handstand push-ups", "Keep the bear crawl moving, even slowly"]'::jsonb,
   '["Start the thrusters at a pace you can repeat five times, since every later movement uses the same muscles.", "Hold the top of the ring dip with your rings turned out to rest between reps.", "Break the push-ups into sets of 5 to 10 before you reach failure, because failed push-ups cost the most time.", "Plan the strict handstand push-ups in sets of 2 or 3 and step down before you miss.", "On the bear crawl, keep your knees an inch off the floor and your back flat."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter barbell or dumbbells for the thrusters. Replace strict ring dips with bench or box dips, push-ups with knee or incline push-ups, and strict handstand push-ups with pike push-ups on a box or dumbbell strict presses. Cut to three rounds if five would take more than about 40 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Pike workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of 20 thrusters (75 lb / 55 lb), 10 strict ring dips, 20 push-ups, 10 strict handstand push-ups and a 50 m bear crawl."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Pike?", "answer": "100 thrusters, 50 strict ring dips, 100 push-ups, 50 strict handstand push-ups and 250 m of bear crawling."}, {"question": "Who was Pike?", "answer": "U.S. Navy Chief Petty Officer Christian Michael Pike, 31, of a Naval Special Warfare unit. He died on March 12, 2013, of combat injuries sustained in Kandahar, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "Can I kip the dips and handstand push-ups?", "answer": "No. CrossFit lists both as strict. If you cannot do them strict, use the scaling options instead."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yO2ajBlHSpw'),
  ('Ralph',
   'ralph',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '4 Rounds For Time',
   '25–35 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','rope','running','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'Ralph honors British Army 2nd Lt. Ralph Johnson, 24, of South Africa, who served with the Household Cavalry Regiment based in Windsor, England. He was killed on Aug. 1, 2006, in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, when insurgents attacked his vehicle with an improvised explosive device.

You complete four rounds of 8 deadlifts (250 lb / 175 lb), 16 burpees, 3 rope climbs to 15 feet and a 600 m run. That adds up to 32 deadlifts, 64 burpees, 12 rope climbs and 2,400 m of running. The heavy pulls and the rope both tax your grip and back, the burpees keep your heart rate high, and the run leaves little time to recover before the bar.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "8", "tip": "Heavy but only eight. Brace before each pull and reset at the floor if your back starts to round.", "rx_men": "250 lb", "rx_women": "175 lb"}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "16", "tip": "Steady pace. Step down and up if jumping spikes your heart rate too high."}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "3", "tip": "Lock your feet on the rope and stand up with your legs to save your arms.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "600 m", "tip": "Use the run to recover your grip. Settle into a pace you can repeat four times."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Save your grip for the rope", "Use your legs on every climb", "Run at a pace you can repeat"]'::jsonb,
   '["Do the deadlifts in sets of 4 or as quick singles, whichever keeps your back flat.", "Use a hook grip or mixed grip on the deadlifts so you save grip for the rope.", "Lock your feet on every rope climb and keep your arms bent only as much as you need.", "Come down the rope hand over hand rather than sliding to protect your hands.", "Start each run easy for the first 100 m, then build to a steady pace."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 155 lb / 105 lb or a weight you can lift for 8 reps with good form. Replace each rope climb with 3 rope pulls from lying on the floor to standing, or 5 strict pull-ups. Cut the run to 400 m if 600 m would take more than about 4 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Ralph workout?", "answer": "4 rounds for time of 8 deadlifts (250 lb / 175 lb), 16 burpees, 3 rope climbs to 15 feet and a 600 m run."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Ralph?", "answer": "32 deadlifts, 64 burpees and 12 rope climbs, plus 2,400 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Ralph?", "answer": "British Army 2nd Lt. Ralph Johnson, 24, of the Household Cavalry Regiment. He was killed on Aug. 1, 2006, in Helmand Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "What can I do instead of rope climbs?", "answer": "Rope pulls from lying to standing, or 5 strict pull-ups per climb, are common substitutes."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IUG4OVdEbgM'),
  ('Rich',
   'rich',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   'For Time',
   '20–30 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','pullUpBar','running']::text[],
   'time',
   'Rich honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Richard Lee Vazquez, 28, of Seguin, Texas, who died on Nov. 13, 2013, of wounds from an improvised explosive device in Panjwai District, Afghanistan. A dedicated CrossFit athlete, he counted snatches, cleans, running, kettlebell swings and pull-ups among his favorite movements.

You start with 13 squat snatches (155 lb / 105 lb), then do 10 rounds of 10 pull-ups and a 100 m sprint, and finish with 13 squat cleans at the same load. The snatches demand speed and mobility while you are fresh. The 100 pull-ups and 1,000 m of sprinting then wear down your grip and legs, so the last 13 cleans are heavy work on tired legs.',
   '[{"name": "Squat Snatches", "reps": "13", "tip": "Quick singles are fine. Catch the bar locked out and stand up tall before you drop it.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Then 10 rounds of 10 pull-ups and a 100 m sprint. Small sets keep your grip ready for the cleans."}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Run fast but not all-out. You have 10 of these."}, {"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "13", "tip": "After the last round. Keep the bar close and meet it in a full front squat.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Singles on the snatches are fine", "Pace the sprints at about 80% effort", "Save some grip for the final cleans"]'::jsonb,
   '["Warm up the squat snatch to your working weight so the first rep is not your first heavy one.", "Drop the bar from overhead and reset each rep, since quick singles are safer than touch-and-go here.", "Break the pull-ups into sets of 5 or 6 in later rounds so you never fail a rep.", "Walk the first few steps back from each sprint and get straight on the bar.", "On the cleans, set your back before every pull and stand up fully before you drop it."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 95 lb / 65 lb, or replace squat snatches with power snatches and squat cleans with power cleans. Use banded or jumping pull-ups, or ring rows. Cut to 6 rounds in the middle if 10 would take more than about 20 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Rich workout?", "answer": "For time: 13 squat snatches, then 10 rounds of 10 pull-ups and a 100 m sprint, then 13 squat cleans. The barbell is 155 lb for men and 105 lb for women."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Rich?", "answer": "13 squat snatches, 100 pull-ups, 1,000 m of sprinting and 13 squat cleans."}, {"question": "Who was Rich?", "answer": "U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Richard Lee Vazquez, 28, of Seguin, Texas. He died on Nov. 13, 2013, of wounds from an improvised explosive device in Panjwai District, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "Why 13 reps?", "answer": "CrossFit does not explain the number. Snatches, cleans, running and pull-ups were among his favorite movements."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=41z2WSsxqPI'),
  ('Ship',
   'ship',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '9 Rounds For Time',
   '25–35 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','box','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'Ship honors Canadian Forces Sgt. Prescott Shipway, 36, of Esterhazy, Saskatchewan, who served with the 2nd Battalion, Princess Patricia''s Canadian Light Infantry, based in Shilo, Manitoba. He was killed on Sept. 7, 2008, by a roadside bomb in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan.

You complete nine rounds of 7 squat cleans (185 lb / 125 lb) and 8 burpee box jumps (36 in / 30 in). That adds up to 63 heavy squat cleans and 72 burpee box jumps. The box is tall, so each jump takes real hip power, and you arrive at the bar breathing hard. Keeping your clean technique sharp through round nine is the challenge.',
   '[{"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "7", "tip": "Quick singles or small sets. Keep the bar close and catch it in a full front squat.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jumps", "reps": "8", "tip": "Burpee facing the box, then jump onto it with both feet. Step down to save your legs.", "rx_men": "36 in", "rx_women": "30 in"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Singles on the cleans keep your form clean", "Step down from the tall box", "Pace for nine rounds, not three"]'::jsonb,
   '["Choose a rhythm for the cleans you can hold for nine rounds, such as a single every 8 to 10 seconds.", "Set your back and push through your whole foot on every clean, even when you are tired.", "After the burpee, step back to the box and jump from a balanced stance rather than rushing.", "Open your hips fully at the top of the box, then step down one foot at a time.", "Take a few breaths before you pick up the bar each round so your first clean is a good one."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 135 lb / 95 lb or a weight you can clean for 7 reps with good form, or use power cleans. Use a 24 in / 20 in box, or step up instead of jumping. Cut to 6 rounds if 9 would take more than about 35 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Ship workout?", "answer": "9 rounds for time of 7 squat cleans (185 lb / 125 lb) and 8 burpee box jumps (36 in / 30 in)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Ship?", "answer": "63 squat cleans and 72 burpee box jumps."}, {"question": "Who was Ship?", "answer": "Canadian Forces Sgt. Prescott Shipway, 36, of the 2nd Battalion, Princess Patricia''s Canadian Light Infantry. He was killed on Sept. 7, 2008, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "Can I step up instead of jumping?", "answer": "Yes. Stepping up and down, or using a lower box, is a common way to scale Ship."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XmzAgTOgDY0'),
  ('T',
   't',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '5 Rounds For Time',
   '25–35 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['running','barbell','kettlebell']::text[],
   'time',
   'T honors Marine Master Sgt. Aaron Torian, 36, of Paducah, Kentucky, of the 2nd Marine Special Operations Battalion, who died on Feb. 15, 2014, during combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, on his sixth deployment. He started CrossFit in 2006 as one of the original members of CrossFit Wilmington, and his favorite movements included cleans, thrusters, sprints and kettlebell swings.

Each of the five rounds is a 100 m sprint, 10 squat clean thrusters (115 lb / 75 lb), 15 kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb), another 100 m sprint and 2 minutes of rest. The rest lets you push each round hard.',
   '[{"name": "Sprint", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Fast but controlled, since the barbell is waiting."}, {"name": "Squat Clean Thrusters", "reps": "10", "tip": "Clean the bar into a full front squat and drive straight up into the press. Each rep starts from the floor.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "15", "tip": "Snap your hips and let the bell float overhead. Keep your arms long.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Second sprint of the round. Push hard, because the rest comes next."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "2 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Walk, breathe and get ready for the next round."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time. Keep the clock running through the rest periods.',
   '["Use the rest to push each round", "Every thruster starts with a clean from the floor", "Long arms and a hip snap on the swings"]'::jsonb,
   '["Treat each round as a hard effort, since you get 2 minutes of rest after it.", "Break the squat clean thrusters into sets of 5 or quick singles to keep good positions.", "Catch the clean in a full squat and use that bounce to drive the bar overhead.", "Keep the kettlebell close to your body at the bottom of each swing to protect your back.", "Walk for the first 30 seconds of each rest, then shake out your arms and get set for the sprint."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 75 lb / 55 lb, or do the cleans and thrusters as separate movements with dumbbells. Use a lighter kettlebell or swing to eye level. Replace sprints with a hard 200 m row if running is not an option.',
   '[{"question": "What is the T workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of a 100 m sprint, 10 squat clean thrusters (115 lb / 75 lb), 15 kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb) and a 100 m sprint, with 2 minutes of rest after each round."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in T?", "answer": "50 squat clean thrusters, 75 kettlebell swings and 1,000 m of sprinting."}, {"question": "Who was T?", "answer": "Marine Master Sgt. Aaron Torian, 36, of the 2nd Marine Special Operations Battalion. He died on Feb. 15, 2014, during combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "What is a squat clean thruster?", "answer": "A clean from the floor caught in a full front squat, then driven straight overhead like a thruster. Each rep starts with the bar on the floor."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7VaAtGHf0RA'),
  ('The Lyon',
   'the-lyon',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '5 Rounds, Each For Time',
   '20–30 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','pullUpBar','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'The Lyon honors Capt. David Lyon, 28, of Sandpoint, Idaho, a member of the 21st Logistics Readiness Squadron at Peterson Air Force Base and a 2008 graduate of the Air Force Academy. He was killed by an improvised explosive device in Kabul, Afghanistan, on Dec. 27, 2013.

Each of the five rounds is 7 squat cleans, 7 shoulder-to-overheads (165 lb / 115 lb) and 7 burpee chest-to-bar pull-ups, done for time, with 2 minutes of rest between rounds. Short rounds and full rest mean each one is a sprint. The heavy barbell and the burpee pull-ups push your heart rate up quickly, and holding your speed across all five rounds is the test.',
   '[{"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "7", "tip": "Quick singles or small sets. Catch the bar in a full front squat.", "rx_men": "165 lb", "rx_women": "115 lb"}, {"name": "Shoulder-to-Overhead", "reps": "7", "tip": "Press, push press or jerk. Finish each rep with locked arms and the bar over your heels.", "rx_men": "165 lb", "rx_women": "115 lb"}, {"name": "Burpee Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "Do a burpee under the bar, jump to it and pull until your chest touches. A bar about 6 inches above your standing reach is ideal."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "2 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Rest between rounds. The clock stops, so recover fully."}]'::jsonb,
   'Time each of the five rounds and add them together for your score. The rest periods do not count.',
   '["Each round is a sprint", "Use the 2 minutes to recover fully", "Chest touches the bar on every pull-up"]'::jsonb,
   '["Go hard from the first rep of each round, since every round is short and followed by rest.", "Clean the bar and go straight to the overhead reps, using a push press or jerk to save your shoulders.", "On the burpee pull-ups, jump to the bar from the bottom of the burpee and pull your chest to it in one motion.", "Set the bar about 6 inches above your standing reach, as CrossFit suggests, so the jump is part of the rep.", "Write down each round time so you can add them up at the end."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 115 lb / 75 lb or a weight you can move for 7 reps with good form. Replace squat cleans with power cleans if needed. Swap burpee chest-to-bar pull-ups for burpee pull-ups (chin over the bar) or burpees plus jumping pull-ups.',
   '[{"question": "What is The Lyon workout?", "answer": "5 rounds, each for time, of 7 squat cleans, 7 shoulder-to-overheads (165 lb / 115 lb) and 7 burpee chest-to-bar pull-ups, with 2 minutes of rest between rounds."}, {"question": "How is The Lyon scored?", "answer": "Time each round and add the five round times together. The rest periods are not counted."}, {"question": "Who was The Lyon?", "answer": "Capt. David Lyon, 28, of Sandpoint, Idaho, a member of the 21st Logistics Readiness Squadron at Peterson Air Force Base. He was killed in Kabul, Afghanistan, on Dec. 27, 2013."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in The Lyon?", "answer": "35 squat cleans, 35 shoulder-to-overheads and 35 burpee chest-to-bar pull-ups."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m5avuKvPB_Y'),
  ('TK',
   'tk',
   'hero',
