   'AMRAP 20',
   'AMRAP 20',
   '20 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['pullUpBar','box','kettlebell']::text[],
   'rounds_reps',
   'TK honors U.S. Army Maj. Thomas E. Kennedy, 35, of West Point, New York, of the 4th Brigade Combat Team, 4th Infantry Division, based in Fort Carson, Colorado. He died on Aug. 8, 2012, of wounds suffered when an insurgent detonated a suicide vest in Kunar Province, Afghanistan.

TK is a 20-minute AMRAP of 8 strict pull-ups, 8 box jumps (36 in / 30 in) and 12 kettlebell swings (70 lb / 53 lb). Every piece is demanding: strict pulling, a tall box and a heavy bell. The pull-ups usually break first, so how you split them decides your score.',
   '[{"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "8", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar. Split the set early."}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "8", "tip": "Tall box, so jump with both feet and step down to save your legs.", "rx_men": "36 in", "rx_women": "30 in"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "12", "tip": "Heavy bell. Snap your hips and keep your arms long all the way overhead.", "rx_men": "70 lb", "rx_women": "53 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps in 20 minutes.',
   '["Split the strict pull-ups before you fail", "Step down from the box", "Heavy bell, strong hip snap"]'::jsonb,
