   'time',
   'Wood honors Australian Army Sgt. Brett Wood MG, 32, of Ferntree Gully, Victoria, who served with the 2nd Commando Regiment based in Sydney. He died on May 23, 2011, in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, after insurgents attacked him with an improvised explosive device.

Each of the five rounds is a 400 m run, 10 burpee box jumps (24 in / 20 in), 10 sumo deadlift high pulls and 10 thrusters (95 lb / 65 lb), followed by 1 minute of rest. That adds up to 2,000 m of running and 50 reps of each movement. The loads are moderate, so the challenge is keeping a fast, steady pace while your heart rate stays high.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Settle into a pace you can hold for five rounds."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jumps", "reps": "10", "tip": "Burpee facing the box, then jump onto it with both feet. Step down to save your legs.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Sumo Deadlift High Pulls", "reps": "10", "tip": "Wide stance, drive with your legs, then pull the bar to chin height with high elbows.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "10", "tip": "Front squat to a full press in one motion. Unbroken if you can.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "1 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Catch your breath before the next run."}]'::jsonb,
