   'rounds_reps',
   'Zimmerman honors U.S. Marine Corps 1st Lt. James R. Zimmerman, 25, of Aroostook, Maine, of the 2nd Battalion, 6th Marine Regiment, 2nd Marine Division, based in Camp Lejeune, North Carolina. He died on Nov. 2, 2010, while conducting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan.

Zimmerman is a 25-minute AMRAP of 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 2 deadlifts (315 lb / 205 lb) and 10 handstand push-ups. The deadlifts are only two reps but very heavy, so they test your back and grip each round. The pull-ups and handstand push-ups then wear down your upper body over 25 minutes. Steady rounds beat a fast start.',
   '[{"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "11", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar. Split the set early to save your grip."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "2", "tip": "Very heavy, but only two. Brace hard and reset at the floor between reps.", "rx_men": "315 lb", "rx_women": "205 lb"}, {"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Head to the floor and arms locked at the top. Break into small sets before you fail."}]'::jsonb,
