   'full-body',
   array['barbell','pullUpBar','box','bodyweight']::text[],
   'total_reps',
   'Jack''s Triangle honors Marine Cpl. Kevin "Jack" Dempsey, 23, of Monroe, Connecticut, of the 2nd Reconnaissance Battalion, 2nd Marine Expeditionary Force, based at Camp Lejeune, North Carolina. He died on Nov. 13, 2004, from wounds sustained by an improvised explosive device while on a reconnaissance foot patrol in Al Anbar Province, Iraq, outside Abu Ghraib.

On a 23-minute clock, you deadlift (225 lb / 155 lb) for max reps for 2 minutes. From 2:00 to 21:00 you do an AMRAP of 4 strict pull-ups, 11 box jumps (30 in / 24 in), 13 hand-release push-ups and a 23-calorie bike. In the final 2 minutes you deadlift again for max reps. Pacing the middle 19 minutes so you still have something for the last deadlift test is the challenge.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "Max reps (0:00–2:00)", "tip": "Two minutes of deadlifts. Pick a pace you can hold, since there is a second deadlift test at the end.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "4", "tip": "From 2:00 to 21:00, AMRAP of this round. No kip; chin clears the bar on every rep."}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "11", "tip": "Jump with both feet and stand tall on top. Step down to save your legs.", "rx_men": "30 in", "rx_women": "24 in"}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "13", "tip": "Chest to the floor, lift your hands, then press back up."}, {"name": "Bike", "reps": "23 cal", "tip": "Steady effort. This is the longest piece of the round."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "Max reps (21:00–23:00)", "tip": "Two more minutes of deadlifts on tired legs. Brace hard and keep your back flat.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total reps across all three parts: both deadlift windows and the 19-minute AMRAP.',
   '["Save something for the final deadlift window", "Keep the bike steady, not all-out", "Have the bar loaded and ready for minute 21"]'::jsonb,
   '["In the first 2 minutes, move at a steady pace of deadlifts you could keep up for the full window.", "Set the bar, box, pull-up bar and bike close together so you lose little time moving between them.", "Split the strict pull-ups if you need to, but never to failure.", "Treat the bike as active recovery for your upper body, with a steady pace you can repeat each round.", "Get to the bar a few seconds before 21:00 so you start the last window on time."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 135 lb / 95 lb or a weight you can lift for steady reps. Use banded strict pull-ups or ring rows, a 24 in / 20 in box or step-ups, and knee push-ups. Cut the bike to 15 calories, or row the same calories, if a bike is not available.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Jack''s Triangle workout?", "answer": "On a 23-minute clock: 2 minutes of max deadlifts, then a 19-minute AMRAP of 4 strict pull-ups, 11 box jumps, 13 hand-release push-ups and a 23-calorie bike, then 2 more minutes of max deadlifts. Loads are 225 lb / 155 lb with a 30 in / 24 in box."}, {"question": "How is Jack''s Triangle scored?", "answer": "Your score is the total reps from both deadlift windows and the 19-minute AMRAP."}, {"question": "Who was Jack?", "answer": "Marine Cpl. Kevin \"Jack\" Dempsey, 23, of Monroe, Connecticut, of the 2nd Reconnaissance Battalion. He died on Nov. 13, 2004, in Al Anbar Province, Iraq."}, {"question": "What equipment do I need for Jack''s Triangle?", "answer": "A barbell, a pull-up bar, a box and a bike for calories."}]'::jsonb,
